"""Versioned public policies. Bump POLICY_VERSION when publishing changes."""
POLICY_VERSION = '2026-11-09'
EFFECTIVE_DATE = 'November 9, 2026'
TERMS = [
('1. About these terms', 'These Terms of Service govern the LionTech Academy website, student portal and related learning services at www.liontechacademy.com. “We” and “us” mean LionTech Academy. By selecting the required acknowledgment during registration, you agree to these terms and acknowledge reading our Privacy Policy. Specific written enrollment agreements and mandatory consumer protections also apply. These terms do not remove rights that cannot lawfully be waived. Contact liontechacademy@gmail.com or WhatsApp +1 437-575-6656 with questions before registering.'),
('2. Eligibility and your account', 'Provide accurate contact, residence and profile information and keep it current. Register only for yourself or with proper authority. You must have legal capacity to enter this agreement; a parent or guardian must contact us to arrange enrollment where required. The portal is not intended for unsupervised registration by children under 13. Do not impersonate others, share accounts or use another student’s number. Your student number identifies your records and payments; it is not a password. Account creation is separate from paid enrollment. Complete required email verification and security steps to activate access.'),
('3. Sign-in and security', 'Keep passwords, verification codes, recovery codes and devices secure. Never send them to support or other students. Available sign-in methods depend on configuration. Two-factor authentication may be required after the displayed grace period, normally seven days after activation, and applies to social sign-in too. Password recovery does not disable two-factor protection. Report suspected unauthorized access promptly. We may restrict access while investigating security concerns or verifying ownership.'),
('4. Programs and access', 'Review the program description, curriculum, delivery format, time zone, start dates and tuition before enrolling. Schedules may change because of instructor availability, holidays or technical and operational issues; we communicate material changes through available notices or contact channels. Check the portal for the current schedule even when using a connected calendar. Account holders can view available program details, schedules, announcements and payment options. Class registration, joining sessions and restricted materials require qualifying verified payment and active approved enrollment for that program or cohort. Payment for one program does not automatically unlock others. No job, income, professional license or third-party certification is guaranteed.'),
('5. Fees, currencies and payments', 'USD is the portal’s base currency. Local-currency equivalents use your residence and available exchange rates; estimates can change. Review the final amount, currency, fees and plan at checkout before payment. Banks and providers may apply conversion or other charges. Enrollment fees and tuition are separate unless expressly stated otherwise; illustrative design examples are not prices. Follow the price and plan offered for your selected program. Payments are linked to your student number, enrollment, invoice and transaction reference. Card payments require provider verification and applicable enrollment checks. Manual receipt submission does not confirm funds: an administrator must verify and approve it. Do not alter receipts or reuse transaction references. Installment access depends on the disclosed plan and payment status.'),
('6. Cancellations, refunds and billing concerns', 'Review program-specific cancellation, refund, withdrawal and installment conditions before purchase. These terms do not create a blanket non-refundable rule, and mandatory statutory refund rights remain available. If specific conditions were not presented, contact us before payment for clarification. For errors, duplicate payments, cancellations or disputes, email your student number, invoice and transaction reference without full card details. We review requests under the applicable enrollment agreement and law. If we cancel a paid program, we communicate available rescheduling, credit or refund options without limiting mandatory rights.'),
('7. Materials, files and intellectual property', 'LionTech or its licensors own course content and branding unless stated otherwise. Active enrollment gives a personal, limited right to use authorized materials for study. Do not redistribute paid content, publish private meeting links, resell materials or bypass access controls. You retain ownership of uploaded work and authorize us to store, display and share it with its intended instructors, administrators or class audience for teaching, assessment and support. Upload only content you may lawfully share. Do not upload malware, unlawful material, unnecessary sensitive records or other people’s information without permission. File limits vary. Keep copies of important work.'),
('8. Conduct and recordings', 'Treat staff and students respectfully. Harassment, discrimination, fraud, cheating and unauthorized system access are prohibited. Cybersecurity exercises require permission from the system owner. Do not record or redistribute sessions or other participants’ images, messages or voices without appropriate permission. If we record a session, the instructor or meeting interface will notify participants and explain the learning purpose. Contact support about concerns or alternatives before a recorded session. Recordings are shared with the intended learning audience unless other use is separately authorized.'),
('9. Communications, integrations and AI', 'We use account details for verification, payment information, class notices and necessary support. Optional marketing and calendar permissions are separate from policy acknowledgment. Connected providers, including social sign-in, payment, meeting and messaging services, have their own terms. Grant permissions only for features you choose. AI assistance may be inaccurate: verify important academic, scheduling and payment information with the portal or staff. Do not enter passwords, card data or unnecessary sensitive information in prompts. AI advice alone does not verify payment or grant access.'),
('10. Availability and restrictions', 'Maintenance, networks and third-party outages can interrupt service. We may update features or restrict accounts for material misuse, security risks, non-payment under an agreed plan or legal requirements. Where practical and appropriate, we explain the reason and provide a way to contact support. We take reasonable steps to operate the service but do not promise uninterrupted or error-free access. Nothing here excludes liability for fraud, deliberate misconduct or liabilities and remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded.'),
('11. Changes, law and contact', 'We publish a new version and effective date when these terms change and notify affected users of material changes through appropriate channels. Renewed agreement is requested where required; prior acknowledgment does not authorize unrelated future uses. Ontario and applicable Canadian law govern, subject to mandatory protections and jurisdiction rights in your place of residence. Contact liontechacademy@gmail.com or WhatsApp +1 437-575-6656 for billing, accessibility, account closure or complaints. Direct support does not replace available legal remedies.'),
]
PRIVACY = [
('1. Responsibility and contact', 'LionTech Academy is responsible for personal information handled through its portal and learning services at www.liontechacademy.com. This policy explains collection, use, sharing and your choices. Email liontechacademy@gmail.com with the subject “Privacy request”, or contact WhatsApp +1 437-575-6656, for questions, access, correction, deletion or complaints. We may verify identity before acting. Do not email passwords, verification codes, full card details or identity documents without an agreed secure process.'),
('2. Information collected', 'Registration information includes name, email, username, phone or WhatsApp number, residence, student type, program choices, language and time zone. We generate a student number and maintain account, enrollment and cohort status. Features you use can generate payment amounts, currencies, invoices, references, verification status, uploaded receipts, coursework, files, attendance or progress records, support inquiries and preferences. We retain the policy versions you acknowledged and acceptance time. Provide only necessary information and remove unrelated financial details from receipts where possible.'),
('3. Security and technical data', 'We handle password hashes, verification and reset challenges, sessions, security events and two-factor enrollment information to protect accounts. Passkeys use public-key credentials: the portal does not receive your device’s fingerprint or facial biometric template. SMS verification providers process your phone number and delivery information. Hosting and security systems may process IP addresses, browser or device details, request times and diagnostic logs for delivery, troubleshooting and abuse prevention. The policy acceptance record itself does not add an IP-address or browser-fingerprint field.'),
('4. Purposes of processing', 'Necessary processing creates and verifies accounts, assigns student numbers, maintains sign-in and recovery, provides programs and materials, reconciles payments, approves enrollment, schedules classes, assesses work, answers inquiries, sends necessary notices, protects the service and meets legal obligations. Residence and preferences localize currency, language and times. Account creation creates an internal support request; authorized staff may use contact and enrollment details to assist you, including via WhatsApp where used. Providing a phone number does not subscribe you to promotional WhatsApp campaigns.'),
('5. Staff and service providers', 'Authorized administrators, instructors and support staff access information relevant to their duties. Hosting, database and private file-storage services process portal records; the portal is hosted on Vercel. When configured and used, Stripe or Flutterwave process checkout and payment status; email services such as SendGrid deliver notices; Twilio and WhatsApp services deliver supported messages or verification; Zoom supports live classes; and Google or Microsoft provide authorized sign-in or calendar features. Not every integration is enabled. A provider receives the data needed for the feature used and may also apply its own privacy policy. We may disclose limited information as legally required or to investigate fraud and protect lawful rights. We do not sell student personal information or publish private receipts and security credentials.'),
('6. Social sign-in and calendars', 'Google or Facebook sign-in provides a provider identifier and authentication profile information such as name and email. Sign-in does not authorize calendar access. Optional calendar connections use the permissions shown by Google or Microsoft to create or update relevant class events; stored connection tokens support those actions. Disconnect or revoke access in provider settings to stop future authorized access. Existing events or retained information may require separate removal. Contact support if portal settings do not offer removal.'),
('7. AI assistance', 'When you submit a question to the portal AI assistant, the prompt and necessary context may be sent to OpenAI if enabled. Student context may include relevant published course information and limited information about your own account or enrollment. Administrator requests may include program or schedule details being edited. Avoid unnecessary sensitive information. Processing and retention depend on the configured API service and its applicable policies; we do not promise zero provider retention. Output can be inaccurate and staff remain responsible for administrative decisions. You can use normal portal functions or contact staff instead of using AI.'),
('8. Classes, uploads and recordings', 'Meeting services may receive display names, email or registration details and participation information. Names, messages, voice, video and screens you share can be visible to participants. Recorded sessions are announced through the instructor or meeting interface and may include participant contributions for the intended learning audience. Publicity and unrelated promotional use require separate permission. Files are shared with their intended class, assignment or staff audience; do not assume class-shared files are visible only to instructors or upload confidential third-party information.'),
('9. Cookies and optional choices', 'Necessary cookies and session storage support sign-in, security, navigation and preferences. Blocking them can prevent account features from working. Third-party pages may use their own cookies. This policy does not authorize optional advertising trackers or analytics cookies: tools requiring consent must be explained and offered separately before use. Necessary security, billing and class notices differ from marketing. Promotional messages require separate appropriate permission and an unsubscribe method. Use available account controls or support to manage optional reminders and calendar connections.'),
('10. International processing and safeguards', 'Providers may process or store information outside your province or country, including outside Canada, where courts and authorities may have access under local law. We use access restrictions, authentication protections, encrypted transport and applicable encrypted storage for sensitive credentials and private records. No online system is completely secure; unauthorized access, disclosure and outages remain possible. We review suspected incidents and provide notifications required by applicable law. Contact us about the providers and international processing relevant to a feature before using it.'),
('11. Retention and closure', 'Records are retained as needed to deliver studies, maintain academic and transaction history, resolve disputes, protect security and meet legal obligations. Periods vary: challenges and sessions expire, while academic, payment, acceptance and audit records may be needed longer. Expiration does not guarantee immediate deletion from every database, backup or provider. Information no longer needed should be deleted, anonymized or securely disposed of under the applicable retention process. Ask support for periods applicable to your records or to close your account. Closure may end learning access. Legitimate legal, accounting and dispute records may remain, and backups may persist until normal replacement.'),
('12. Access, correction and withdrawal', 'You can request information about processing, access to your information, correction, and deletion or restriction where applicable. You may withdraw optional permissions or ask about withdrawing consent for necessary processing; withdrawal of necessary processing may prevent account operation or selected services. We explain consequences and lawful limits. Additional rights such as portability or objection may apply by location. We respond within applicable legal deadlines and explain permitted exceptions. You can complain to us or the appropriate regulator, including the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada at priv.gc.ca. Optional marketing and calendar access are not conditions of account creation.'),
('13. Young students and changes', 'The portal is not intended for unsupervised registration by children under 13. A parent or guardian should contact us before arranging enrollment for a child or learner unable to give meaningful consent. We adapt consent and communications to capacity and applicable law. Tell us if a child’s data was submitted without appropriate authorization. We publish updates with their version and date and notify affected users of material changes. New purposes or optional disclosures requiring consent are presented separately where required; prior acknowledgment is not blanket permission for unrelated future processing.'),
]
